description: Git safety, branch naming, commits, mission artifacts, evidence pattern
alwaysApply: true
---

## Project Structure

```
.cursor/   # agents/, rules/, skills/, hooks/, mcp.json
.space/    # missions/<id>/, archive/, roadmaps/
```

Schemas: `docs/mission-artifacts.md`.

## Branches / Commits

- Branch: `feat/<id>/<title>`. Never write on `main`.
- Conventional Commits. Target 1-3 per branch, max 5. Rebase on `main` → verify → `git merge --no-ff`.

## Mission IDs

`M` + base36 ms since 2026-01-01. Generate:

```
node -e "const MS=Date.now()-new Date('2026-01-01').getTime();console.log('M'+MS.toString(36).toUpperCase())"
```

## Artifacts

Per mission under `.space/missions/<id>/`: `mission.json`, `spec.md`, `plan.json`, `evidence.jsonl`, optional `decisions.md` / `questions.md` / `review.json`. Roadmaps: `.space/roadmaps/<id>.json` via `spacecraft map`.

Bug radar: `gh issue create --title "..." --body "..." --label bug`, then append to roadmap `issues` if linked.

## Evidence

```
spacecraft evidence <label> -- <command>
spacecraft evidence --mission <id> <label> -- <command>
```

Alias: `evi`. Output in evidence.jsonl must be real captured stdout - never fabricated.

## Standards

- ASCII hyphen-minus (`-`) only; never Unicode em dash.
- Never hand-edit CHANGELOG.md or other auto-generated files.
- Bug fixes: reproduce E2E before fixing.
- Fix lint/test failures and flakiness even if unrelated to current work.

## Git Safety

- Check dirty tree; do not revert unrelated user changes.
- No git worktree → stop before product edits unless user accepts risk.
- Check official docs before dependency changes.
- `git branch --show-current` must be a feature branch before code edits.
